### OAuth2 API Testing
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@email = testuser@example.com
@password = password123
@username = testuser

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Get Available Endpoints
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/endpoints

### 3. User Registration
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "full_name": "Test User"
}

### 4. User Login (Get JWT Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 5. Get User Profile (Protected - Need JWT Token from login)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 6. Create OAuth Client (Protected - Need JWT Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/clients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "name": "Test OAuth Client",
  "description": "OAuth client for testing",
  "redirect_uris": ["http://localhost:3000/callback"],
  "scopes": ["read", "write"],
  "grant_types": ["authorization_code", "refresh_token"]
}

### 7. Get OAuth Clients List (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/clients
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 8. OAuth Authorization Endpoint (Step 1 - Get Authorization Code)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3000/callback&scope=read&state=random_state_string

### 9. OAuth Token Exchange (Step 2 - Exchange Code for Access Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&code=YOUR_AUTHORIZATION_CODE&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3000/callback&client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID&client_secret=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET

### 10. OAuth UserInfo Endpoint (Using Access Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 11. OAuth Discovery Endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/.well-known/openid-configuration

### 12. Token Introspection (RFC 7662)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/introspect
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

token=YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_TO_INSPECT

### 13. Admin Dashboard (Admin Only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 14. Admin - Get Users (Admin Only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/users?limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 15. Admin - Update User Status (Admin Only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/users/USER_ID_HERE/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "is_active": false
}

### 16. Admin - Update User Role (Admin Only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/users/USER_ID_HERE/role
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "role": "admin"
}

### 17. Admin - Get System Events (Admin Only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/events?limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 18. Refresh Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "refresh_token": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

### 19. Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 20. Change Password (Protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "current_password": "{{password}}",
  "new_password": "newpassword123"
}

### Example OAuth Flow Test (Complete Flow)
### Step 1: Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "oauthuser",
  "email": "oauth@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "full_name": "OAuth Test User"
}

### Step 2: Login to get JWT token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "oauth@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Step 3: Create OAuth client (use JWT from step 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/clients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer JWT_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2

{
  "name": "Test App",
  "description": "Test OAuth Application",
  "redirect_uris": ["http://localhost:3000/callback"],
  "scopes": ["read", "write"],
  "grant_types": ["authorization_code", "refresh_token"]
}

### Step 4: Simulate OAuth Authorization (use client_id from step 3)
### In browser: http://localhost:8080/api/auth/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=CLIENT_ID&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3000/callback&scope=read&state=xyz

### Step 5: Exchange authorization code for access token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&code=AUTHORIZATION_CODE&redirect_uri=http://localhost:3000/callback&client_id=CLIENT_ID&client_secret=CLIENT_SECRET

### Step 6: Use access token to get user info
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/oauth/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_5